/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 42 0 R
/E (Diffie-Hellman lets two parties agree on a shared secret over a public channel without ever sending the secret itself. Both sides agree on a public prime p and a primitive root \(generator\) g. Each side picks a private random number, computes a public value from it, and exchanges only that public value. Because discrete logarithms are hard to reverse, an eavesdropper who sees p, g and both public values still cannot efficiently recover the private numbers or the shared secret. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [21]
